  "emphasis": {
    "primary": "Damage (Crystal burst on all three attacks, +5 ceiling)",
    "secondary": "Increase Damage Taken (Crystal Sphere and Crystal Cave exposure, two rows, +7 ceiling)",
    "tertiary": "Decrease Damage Taken (Crystal Sphere, +10 ceiling) and Reflect (Crystal Cave, +10 ceiling), with Increase Damage Given as route glue (+5 ceiling on Kōsai Shippū)",
    "rationale": "Crystal Essence is a rank-A Defensive / Sustained Damage kit with eight supported rows on five tags. Three of its five jutsu carry a Crystal damage row (Prism 50, Kōsai Shippū 40, Crystal Cave 40, all 60 AP / cooldown 7), so raw Crystal power is the primary emphasis and the deepest offensive commitment. Its two Increase Damage Taken rows (Sphere single target, Cave area enemies, both 35% for two rounds) anchor an exposure route, while the 40 AP Crystal Sphere's 35% Decrease Damage Taken and the Cave's 40% Reflect each anchor a defensive route that honours the Defensive trait. Increase Damage Given has a single row (Shippū 35%, self) whose matching hits the bloodline IDG passive already multiplies, so it stays Foundation and capstone-secondary glue capped at +5 rather than earning a route."
  },
